  "causebase_summary": "5D Clinics Foundation Ltd (5D Clinics Foundation) is presented on its website as an organisation that aims to provide “access to world class cancer treatment for everyone.” The website states the foundation consults with clinical experts who “have access to the full suite of resources available for cancer care” and that it “financially assist[s] patients with the most appropriate treatment specific to their needs.” The organisation frames its activity around supporting people after a cancer diagnosis and says it seeks to reduce fear of the unknown during a patient’s cancer journey. Regulatory records include an ACNC register extract and an ACNC AIS filing for 01/07/2022–30/06/2023 reporting revenue of AUD 220,477 and total expenses of AUD 217,456. The organisation’s listed geography includes Western Australia. The available evidence is primarily the organisation’s website text and an AIS financial extract; the website statements are organisation-authored claims and the AIS provides basic financials but does not report numbers of people assisted, eligibility criteria, detailed service models, or staff and volunteer arrangements.",
